{
  "format": "zapterm-command-lists",
  "version": 1,
  "platform": "fortimanager",
  "notes": "FortiManager 7.6 command lists. Every command was checked against the FortiManager 7.6.0 CLI reference (docs.fortinet.com/document/fortimanager/7.6.0/cli-reference): get system, diagnose dvm (140839), diagnose fgfm, diagnose fmupdate, diagnose ha, diagnose fmnetwork, diagnose system, diagnose sniffer, execute. Read-only commands only. Left out on purpose: diagnose dvm task repair/reset and taskline repair (“The FortiManager will reboot”), diagnose dvm check-integrity and diagnose cdb check (they offer to change the database; the 7.6.5 upgrade guide warns check-integrity can corrupt the device database on 7.4.8), every delete, reset, reload, force-resync and fmupdate update/restart command. The sniffer carries a caution quoting the sniffer reference (“Packet capture can be very resource intensive”) and its count is limited to 1–1000.",
  "label": "FortiManager · 7.6",
  "stopDebug": [],
  "stopKeys": "\u0003",
  "lists": [
    {
      "id": "system",
      "name": "System",
      "icon": "system",
